//@version=5
strategy("RSI Mean Reversion Fade", overlay=true)

// T58_SL_PIPS=30
// T58_TP_PIPS=45
//
// NEW STRATEGY (built from scratch, 2026-08-30) -- pure counter-trend
// mean reversion. Deliberately the OPPOSITE mechanism from the prior Pine
// file in this library (ema_trend_rsi_pullback.pine traded WITH an
// established trend; this one fades price with no trend filter at all).
// Written strictly inside T58's supported Pine subset -- only ta.rsi,
// plain comparisons over it, no security()/custom functions/arrays/other
// ta.* calls (see app/strategy/pinescript.py / STRATEGY_FORMAT.md).
//
// MECHANISM: enter when RSI reaches a genuine extreme (<25 or >75) --
// betting price has moved too far, too fast, and is due to mean-revert.
// The exit is ACTIVE: once RSI recovers back through the 50 midline, the
// move this trade was betting on is considered played out, so it closes
// rather than waiting on the fixed stop/target. The 30/45-pip stop/target
// below is a backstop for the cases where price keeps running against
// the fade -- it should rarely be what actually closes a winning trade.
//
// KNOWN LIMITATION (not fixable within this parser subset): the
// stop/target MUST be expressed as fixed pips here -- Pine's restricted
// subset has no ATR/dynamic-stop primitive available. That means the
// 30/45 values below are only correctly SIZED once you set the Risk
// tab's pip_size to match whatever instrument you're testing (0.01 for
// gold/JPY pairs, 0.0001 for most other FX pairs) -- or use the app's
// "detect pip size from data" button before running this on a new
// instrument. This is a structural property of the Pine parser subset,
// not something a strategy file can route around.
//
// NOT YET VALIDATED: this has not been run through T58's Full Pipeline.
// No GA search, no walk-forward, no Monte Carlo, no significance gate --
// treat 25/75/50 and the pip values as a starting point for the GA to
// refine, not a finished, tested setting.

rsiVal = ta.rsi(close, 14)

longCondition = rsiVal < 25
shortCondition = rsiVal > 75
exitLongCondition = rsiVal > 50
exitShortCondition = rsiVal < 50

if longCondition
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long)
if shortCondition
    strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short)

strategy.close("Long", when=exitLongCondition)
strategy.close("Short", when=exitShortCondition)
